              Reference transcripts

These are the transcripts the three original Scheme implementations of
Thomas produced from ../../dylan-examples.dyl, kept as the regression
baseline for the Common Lisp version.  They came from

    kits/MIT/dylan-examples.output      -> MIT.output
    kits/gambit/dylan-examples.output   -> gambit.output
    kits/scc/dylan-examples.output      -> scc.output

before those directories were removed.  MIT.output is the one the Common
Lisp version is compared against: MIT CScheme was the platform Thomas was
developed on, and it is the Scheme whose treatment of #F and '() the class
heterarchy assumes.

To regenerate the Common Lisp transcript:

    $ sbcl
    * (load "load-dylan.lisp")
    * (load "full-test.lisp")
    * (dylan:test-examples)

Compare it against MIT.output from the "(test ..." line onwards, ignoring
#[...] object representations and blank lines.  As of the translation the
two agree on every value except the handful of differences listed under
"DIFFERENCES FROM THE SCHEME VERSION" in ../README -- and the gambit and
scc transcripts are kept here because they disagree with MIT.output, and
with each other, on exactly those points.

The head of each file carries the Digital Equipment Corporation copyright
notice that applies to all of Thomas.  See ../../LICENSE.
